WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.400
One tap, and the forest wakes up. Softly.

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:16.400
Louder, quieter: the volume glides, it never jumps.

3
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.600
Stop: the sound fades away. It is never cut.

4
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.600
One card, one finger. Now, the whole table.

5
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.400
Music, ambiences and events, each in its row.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:49.600
Layer them as the story moves: birds, a raven, an owl.

7
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.600
A new chapter: the forest fades out, the bear's chapter rises.

8
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:13.000
The calm before the storm, the wind, the roar, the claws. A few taps.

9
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.400
One tap ends the scene. Everything fades out together.

10
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.600
Troubadour Map: every sound lives in a place.

11
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.600
Press and hold to set the party down. The forest rises around it.

12
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:43.600
Drag the party: the sounds follow it, place after place. Here, the creek.

13
00:01:44.800 --> 00:02:01.000
Up to the bear's den. The wind turns restless, the bear growls.

14
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:13.000
Down to the pub. Its music takes over by itself.

15
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:20.400
Troubadour Ballade: the scene, written in advance.

16
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:30.000
Begin: the first step plays, and the next ones follow on time.

17
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:42.400
You keep your eyes on the players. The Ballade keeps the time.

18
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:51.600
Go: the bear charges.

19
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.600
Go: the bear falls. Fanfare.
